IMPORT prelude

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Commonwealth), compilation C2026C00425: the nouns of Chapter 2 Parts 2-1 to 2-3 Division 4.
-- Declarations only. A fact a witness could state about the person, the child, a day or a determination goes here;
-- whether those facts meet a rule of the Act is decided in the module of the Part that states the rule.
-- Every field is a plain fact. A field named after a rule of the PPL rules or of another Act is asked as a fact,
-- because those instruments are not among the sources.

-- How the person stands to the child (the Dictionary's "parent", section 13(3)-(4), section 15(1)).
DECLARE `The parental relationship` HAS
    `the child was adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child was born because of an artificial conception procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child was born because of a surrogacy arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an adoptive parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a parent of the child under section 60H of the Family Law Act 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a parent of the child under section 60HB of the Family Law Act 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a parent of the child in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the child's birth mother` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the partner of the child's birth mother` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the partner of an adoptive parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the partner of a person covered by section 13(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A permission to claim flexible PPL days for a child (section 15).
DECLARE `A permission to claim flexible PPL days` HAS
    `a permission has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the permission has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission` IS A NUMBER

-- The facts section 13(2) reads when the Secretary decides a PPL claim.
DECLARE `The facts for a determination under section 13(2)` HAS
    `the claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on the claimed days` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the child's birth mother has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child's birth mother satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `an adoptive parent of the child has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person who gave the claimant the permission referred to in subparagraph 13(2)(e)(i) satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(d) apply to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(e) apply to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a payability determination under section 13 is in force in relation to another adoptive parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the permission given to the claimant under paragraph 15(1)(a)` IS A `A permission to claim flexible PPL days`
    `the permission given to the claimant under paragraph 15(1)(b) or (c)` IS A `A permission to claim flexible PPL days`
    `the number of flexible PPL days for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person if the determination were made` IS A NUMBER

-- The facts section 14(2) reads when the Secretary decides a special PPL claim.
DECLARE `The facts for a determination under section 14(2)` HAS
    `a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable to a PPL claimant is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the special PPL claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on the claimed days` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the permission given to the special PPL claimant under subsection 15(2)` IS A `A permission to claim flexible PPL days`
    `the number of flexible PPL days for which parental leave pay would be payable to the special PPL claimant if the determination were made` IS A NUMBER

-- A day claimed in a PPL claim or special PPL claim, with whether the Secretary is satisfied of the matters in section 13(2) or 14(2) for it.
DECLARE `A claimed day` HAS
    `the day claimed` IS A DATE
    `the Secretary is satisfied of the matters for the day` IS A BOOLEAN

-- One day of a person's work test period (sections 32 to 36).
DECLARE `A day in the work test period` HAS
    `hours of paid work performed` IS A NUMBER
    `hours of paid leave taken` IS A NUMBER
    `a flexible PPL day for a previous child on which parental leave pay was payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a jobkeeper payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours taken for a jobkeeper payment period day under the PPL rules` IS A NUMBER
    `in a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours taken for a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period day under the PPL rules` IS A NUMBER

-- The facts about a claimant on one flexible PPL day that sections 31AA and 31AB read.
DECLARE `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day` HAS
    `satisfies the Australian residency test on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is caring for the child on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of paid work performed on the day` IS A NUMBER
    `has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the work test on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the income test on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the Australian residency test on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the child was born is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period the person is subject to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies to the person on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child is stillborn or has died before the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would have been caring for the child on the day had the child not been stillborn or died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a special PPL claim can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AA(4)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AA(5)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant's partner satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a partner at the time of making the first effective claim in relation to the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AB(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AB(5)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `flexible PPL days covered by determinations in force for any person` IS A NUMBER
    `flexible PPL days covered by determinations in force for the claimant or the claimant's partner` IS A NUMBER
    `flexible PPL days covered by determinations under section 13 in force for the claimant` IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant is deceased on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period for the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies to the claimant on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `flexible PPL days covered by determinations under section 13 or 14 in force for the claimant` IS A NUMBER
